null,"type_line":"Instant"},{"cmc":3.0,"color_identity":["U","W"],"colors":["W"],"defense":null,"keywords":["Flanking"],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"not_legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{2}{W}","name":"Teferi's Honor Guard","oracle_id":"8a3a8a02-b7da-4648-a772-c9efb7c332da","oracle_text":"Flanking (Whenever a creature without flanking blocks this creature, the blocking creature gets -1/-1 until end of turn.)\n{U}{U}: This creature phases out. (While it's phased out, it's treated as though it doesn't exist. It phases in before you untap during your next untap step.)","power":"2","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"1997-02-03","toughness":"2","type_line":"Creature — Human Knight"},{"cmc":5.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"banned","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"banned","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"banned","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{3}{U}{U}","name":"Time Warp","oracle_id":"dbd6a94b-62ff-4a10-9d52-bdd90b26e425","oracle_text":"Target player takes an extra turn after this one.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2026-06-26","toughness":null,"type_line":"Sorcery"},{"cmc":3.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"not_legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{2}{U}","name":"Vodalian Illusionist","oracle_id":"ac935639-ba30-4b04-86f6-363527e85a8b","oracle_text":"{U}{U}, {T}: Target creature phases out. (While it's phased out, it's treated as though it doesn't exist. It phases in before its controller untaps during their next untap step.)","power":"2","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"1997-06-09","toughness":"2","type_line":"Creature — Merfolk Wizard"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"An attacking or blocking creature that phases out is removed from combat.","oracle_id":"02a7d95a-0a45-4aa3-b5b8-01c0b36462d8","published_at":"2021-07-23","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Any continuous effects with a \"for as long as\" duration, such as that of Mind Flayer, ignore phased-out objects. If ignoring those objects causes the effect's conditions to no longer be met, the duration will expire.","oracle_id":"02a7d95a-0a45-4aa3-b5b8-01c0b36462d8","published_at":"2021-07-23","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"As Blink Dog phases out, Auras and Equipment attached to it also phase out at the same time. Those Auras and Equipment will phase in at the same time Blink Dog does, and they'll phase in still attached to Blink Dog.","oracle_id":"02a7d95a-0a45-4aa3-b5b8-01c0b36462d8","published_at":"2021-07-23","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Choices made for permanents as they entered the battlefield are remembered when they phase in.","oracle_id":"02a7d95a-0a45-4aa3-b5b8-01c0b36462d8","published_at":"2021-07-23","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an opponent gains control of your Blink Dog, activates its Teleport ability, and the duration of the control-change effect expires before it phases in, Blink Dog phases in under your control as that opponent's next untap step begins. If they leave the game before their next untap step, Blink Dog phases in as the next untap step begins after their turn would have begun.","oracle_id":"02a7d95a-0a45-4aa3-b5b8-01c0b36462d8","published_at":"2021-07-23","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Permanents phase back in during their controller's untap step, immediately before that player untaps their permanents. Creatures that phase in this way are able to attack and pay a cost of {T} during that turn. If a permanent had counters on it when it phased out, it will have those counters when it phases back in.","oracle_id":"02a7d95a-0a45-4aa3-b5b8-01c0b36462d8","published_at":"2021-07-23","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Phased out permanents are treated as though they don't exist. They can't be the target of spells or abilities, their static abilities have no effect on the game, their triggered abilities can't trigger, they can't attack or block, and so on.","oracle_id":"02a7d95a-0a45-4aa3-b5b8-01c0b36462d8","published_at":"2021-07-23","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Phasing out doesn't cause any \"leaves the battlefield\" abilities to trigger. Similarly, phasing in won't cause any \"enters the battlefield\" abilities to trigger.","oracle_id":"02a7d95a-0a45-4aa3-b5b8-01c0b36462d8","published_at":"2021-07-23","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once the exiled permanent returns, it's considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners' graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The returned card won't be the target of any spells or abilities that targeted it before. Any spells that don't target, such as Akroma's Vengeance, will still affect it.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"When an effect returns the exiled card \"under your control,\" you control it indefinitely after that. In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, any creatures you control from Cloudshift's effect are exiled.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
